@@ -70,6 +70,19 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts its objects to plain text, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. It does the following:
+
+- Does not pretty print containers or objects; each object is converted with normal string conversion.
+- Does not wrap or crop the output to the console width.
+- Does not process console markup or emoji codes; square brackets and emoji codes are written literally.
+- Applies highlighting by default, which can be turned off with ``highlight=False``, and applies an optional basic ``style``.
+
+Output still goes through the console's render hooks and buffer, like print output.
+
+
 Justify / Alignment
